# im an obsessive learner — for domain glyphs 📜

zoom-in of `im_an.obsessive_learner`: the **glyph lesson**. a glyph is a term on a surface with no room for a word; one concept, one symbol. lands in `domain.glyphs/catalog.of=glyph._.md` + `catalog.of=glyph.axis=$axis.md`.

failures: two glyphs for one concept · one glyph for two concepts · a glyph claimed with no record.

a grep proves a glyph UNUSED, never UNCLAIMED.

| when… | then… |
|---|---|
| you claim a glyph, on any axis | catalog it: the row IS the claim |
| it is not in the repo's palette | add it first, with its sense |
| a grep returns no match | unused, not unclaimed: read the catalog |
| a grep hits several surfaces | one concept seen twice · decoration · or two concepts (only the last blocks) |
| a glyph is in use with no row | add the row now |
| two copies of the record disagree | reconcile to the catalog |
| you coin a third glyph for a concept a marker covers | reuse the settled one |

test, before the claim: *1. does this glyph name what its subject DOES? 2. what CONCEPT does it hold, and does another glyph hold it?* picked for looks fails 1; a held concept fails 2 → reuse.

then update every published face that restates the catalog. see `domain.terms/term=glyph._.choice._.md`.
